From: IMX6ULL AV Project <learning-project@local>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov5640: use 1x DVP output drive strength

The NXP 4.1.15 OV5640 driver programs register 0x302c[7:6] for 2x
output drive strength after every mode initialization.  On the ALIENTEK
i.MX6ULL camera interface, VGA YUYV at 30 fps showed motion-dependent line
displacement with 2x drive strength.  Raising the setting to 3x and 4x made
the displacement progressively worse, while 1x removed it completely.

The 1x setting was validated with 54,000 dynamically changing frames at
30.02 fps.  There were no driver sequence gaps, timeouts, stale-frame drops
or CSI errors, and register readback after capture still reported 1x.

This monotonic dependence on output drive is consistent with excessive
edge rate causing overshoot, ringing or crosstalk on this board-level DVP
connection.  Keep the CSI receiver on its proven rising PCLK edge and use
the lowest stable OV5640 drive setting.

---
 drivers/media/platform/mxc/capture/ov5640.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mxc/capture/ov5640.c b/drivers/media/platform/mxc/capture/ov5640.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mxc/capture/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mxc/capture/ov5640.c
@@ -1062,10 +1062,16 @@ static int ov5640_init_mode(void)
 	if (retval < 0)
 		goto err;
 
-	/* change driver capability to 2x according to validation board.
-	 * if the image is not stable, please increase the driver strength.
+	/*
+	 * The ALIENTEK i.MX6ULL parallel DVP connection is stable at 1x.
+	 * VGA/30-fps motion tests showed line displacement at 2x; 3x and 4x
+	 * made it progressively worse.  A 54,000-frame dynamic test at 1x
+	 * completed at 30.02 fps without visual corruption, sequence gaps,
+	 * timeouts or CSI errors.  The monotonic drive-strength dependence
+	 * points to excessive edge rate and board-level signal integrity,
+	 * so do not use the original validation-board value of 2x here.
 	 */
-	ov5640_driver_capability(2);
+	ov5640_driver_capability(1);
 	ov5640_set_bandingfilter();
 	ov5640_set_AE_target(AE_Target);
 	ov5640_set_night_mode(night_mode);
-- 
2.7.4
